WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:04.630
The mystery behind Rey's parentage has buzzed
around in Star Wars fans' minds since director

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:10.080
J.J. Abrams' The Force Awakens introduced
us to Daisy Ridley's scrappy Jakku-born scavenger.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.460
We learned via a mysterious "Force vision"
that Rey's parents orphaned her as a child,

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:17.600
though audiences never learned their names
or saw their faces.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:18.500
Who are they?

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:22.760
Rian Johnson's The Last Jedi offered up an
answer, if Adam Driver's Kylo Ren is to be

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:26.980
believed: Rey's parents were insignificant,
low-life junkers who sold her for drinking

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:27.560
money.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.320
But apparently that's not what Abrams had
in mind when he was considering how to answer

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.800
the question of Rey's parentage.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:37.020
According to actor Simon Pegg, who played
Unkar Plutt in The Force Awakens, Abrams'

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.700
plan was different than what we saw in The
Last Jedi.

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:45.360
Pegg hinted at Abram's intentions on MTV correspondent
Josh Horowitz's Happy Sad Confused podcast.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:51.600
"I know what J.J. kind of intended, or at
least what was sort of being chucked around.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:55.830
I think that's kind of been undone slightly
by the last one."

00:00:55.830 --> 00:01:03.260
"There was some talk about, you know, a kind
of relevant lineage for her.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.160
But I don't know, and I don't know if anybody
knows."

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:10.360
There are still a ton of theories floating
around, but whether Abrams meant for the trilogy

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.840
to eventually reveal Rey as a descendant of
the Skywalker clan or a member of the Kenobi

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.880
family tree, or something else altogether,
remains a mystery.

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:22.140
But Pegg's comment reveals at the very least
that Abrams' intentions weren't in line with

00:01:22.159 --> 00:01:24.909
Johnson's later handling of the parentage
question.

00:01:24.909 --> 00:01:29.590
Still, this all hinges on the assumption that
Johnson intended Kylo Ren's explanation to

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:30.120
be truthful.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:34.180
There's evidence to the contrary: Johnson
previously revealed that "anything's still

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.340
open" when it comes to who Rey really is and
where she truly came from.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:41.380
Just as Johnson took over the story from Abrams
after The Force Awakens, Abrams is grabbing

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:45.060
the baton and stepping back into the director's
seat for Episode 9.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.980
Abrams may very well undo what was revealed
in The Last Jedi, delivering a twist that

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:53.660
allows his original vision for Rey's origins,
whatever that may be, to come full circle.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:57.710
After all, Kylo Ren may just have lied and
told the clearly powerful Rey that she's a

00:01:57.710 --> 00:02:02.380
nobody from a family of "filthy junk traders"
to get her to join him in his twisted galactic

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:02.900
conquest.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:07.360
The truth may be a whole lot more hopeful,
and will hopefully be revealed when Star Wars:

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:10.600
Episode 9 is released on December 20th, 2019.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:12.080
Thanks for watching!

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.620
